5417] [17592186174738 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174738 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174738 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186498212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174738 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "219bd34f-9e71-5315-809c-74bdaa997dcb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175733 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14143" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175733 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $\\dfrac{2}{1-2k}=-\\dfrac{4}{3k}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175733 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1be25af9-d59f-5270-b9e1-d0c5dcd731e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175733 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $k=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $k=0$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{2}{1-2k}&=-\\dfrac{4}{3k}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{2}{1-2k}&=\\dfrac{-4}{3k}\\[5pt]\n\t\t2 \\cdot 3k &= (-4) \\cdot (1-2k)\\[5pt]\t\t\n\t\t6k&=-4+8k\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\t\n\t\t6k&=-4+8k\\[5pt]\n\t\t6k-8k &=-4+8k-8k\\[5pt]\n\t\t-2k&=-4\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{-2k}{-2} &= \\dfrac{-4}{-2} \\[5pt]\n\t\tk &= 2\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince  $k =   2$ is different from $k=0$ and $k=\\dfrac{1}{2}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $k=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175734 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175734 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{2}{4x+12}=\\dfrac{2}{x+3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175734 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "72cf8733-9727-5a9f-8028-1dee62e5715d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175734 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=-3$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\dfrac{2}{4x+12} &= \\dfrac{2}{x+3} \\\t\n\t2 \\cdot (x+3) &= (4x+12) \\cdot 2 \\\n\t2x + 6 &= 8x + 24\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2x + 6 &= 8x + 24 \\\n\t2x + 6-24 &= 8x + 24-24 \\\n\t2x-18 &= 8x \\\n\t2x-18-2x &= 8x-2x \\\n\t-18 &= 6x \\\n        \\dfrac{-18}{6} &= \\dfrac{6x}{6} \\\n        -3 &= x\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-3$ cannot be a solution, the equation has **no solutions.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175739 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175739 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $x$ where $-\\dfrac{3}{2x}=\\dfrac{2}{x+7}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175739 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d5b690c-bee9-5503-8f21-285b8c42d5fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175739 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=0$ and $x=-7$  cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t-\\dfrac{3}{2x}&=\\dfrac{2}{x+7}\\[5pt]\t\n        \\dfrac{-3}{2x}&=\\dfrac{2}{x+7}\\[5pt]\t\n\t(-3) \\cdot (x+7) &=2x \\cdot (2) \\[5pt]\t\n\t-3x - 21&=  4x\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t-3x - 21&= 4x\\[5pt]\t\n\t-3x -21 + 3x&=4x + 3x\\[5pt]\t\n\t-21&=7x\\[5pt]\t\n\t\\dfrac{-21}{7}&=\\dfrac{7x}{7} \\[5pt]\t\n\t-3 &= x\n\t}\n$$\n\nSince  $x =   - 3$ is different from $x=0$ and $x=-7$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x= -3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175906 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175906 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175906 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175906 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186498538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175906 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186498554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175906 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Rational Equations Containing a Binomial in One Denominator" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175