"q-215066" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498505 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498505 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{4}{3x-5}=-\\frac{2}{x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498505 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22fb2eb0-0b37-5e4e-b13e-bbd075981dde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498505 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=0$  cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3x-5} & =-\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3x-5} & =\\frac{-2}{x} \\\\ 4\\cdot x & =(3x-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 4x & =-6x+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =-6x+10 \\\\ 4x+6x & =-6x+10+6x \\\\ 10x & =10 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & =\\frac{10}{10} \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=1$ is different from $x=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=0,$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498538 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498538 #edb/ref 1069 "q-214969" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498538 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498538 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $z$ where $\\frac{4}{3z-4}=\\frac{2}{z}.$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55ccf1ca-e318-559b-93b2-d5adb07323fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498538 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $z=0$ and $z=\\frac{4}{3}$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3z-4} & =\\frac{2}{z} \\\\ 4\\cdot z & =(3z-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 4z & =6z-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z & =6z-8 \\\\ 4z-6z & =6z-8-6z \\\\ -2z & =-8 \\\\ \\frac{-2z}{-2} & =\\frac{-8}{-2} \\\\ z & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z=4$ is different from $z=0$ and $z=\\frac{4}{3}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $z=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498554 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498554 #edb/ref 1069 "q-47793" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498554 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498554 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{3}{2x}=\\frac{4}{3x-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498554 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e6d0052-ede1-5485-af6f-3596ff037aef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498554 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2x} & =\\frac{4}{3x-1} \\\\ 3\\cdot (3x-1) & =(2x)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 9x-3 & =8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3 & =8x \\\\ 9x-3-9x & =8x-9x \\\\ -3 & =-x \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-1} & =\\frac{-x}{-1} \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=3$ is different from $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3},$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is  $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498563 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498563 #edb/ref 1069 "q-51492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498563 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498563 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\frac{5}{4x+24}=\\frac{5}{x+6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498563 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93eae023-b2fa-5964-961a-3ebb3b808918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498563 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=-6$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4x+24} & =\\frac{5}{x+6} \\\\ 5\\cdot (x+6) & =(4x+24)\\cdot 5 \\\\ 5x+30 & =20x+120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+30 & =20x+120 \\\\ 5x+30-5x & =20x+120-5x \\\\ 30 & =15x+120 \\\\ 30-120 & =15x+120-120 \\\\ -90 & =15x \\\\ \\frac{-90}{15} & =\\frac{15x}{15} \\\\ -6 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-6$ cannot be a solution, the equation has no solutions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498568 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498568 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215142" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498568 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498568 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{2}{x+8}=\\frac{3}{5-2x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498568 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f1e58eb-509a-57ef-98db-701046002754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498568 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $x=-8$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{x+8} & =\\frac{3}{5-2x} \\\\ 2\\cdot (5-2x) & =(x+8)\\cdot 3 \\\\ 10-4x & =3x+24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-4x & =3x+24 \\\\ 10-4x+4x & =3x+24+4x \\\\ 10 & =7x+24 \\\\ 10-24 & =7x+24-24 \\\\ -14 & =7x \\\\ \\frac{-14}{7} & =\\frac{7x}{7} \\\\ -2 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-2$ is different from $x=-8$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2},$ we can accept it as a solution. Therefore, the solution is $x=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498588 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498588 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215111" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498588 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498588 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $y$ where $\\frac{3}{y}=-\\frac{2}{y+5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df156dc2-1100-5e24-8d9b-7d140c269cdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498588 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $y=0$ and $y=-5$  cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{y} & =-\\frac{2}{y+5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{y} & =\\frac{-2}{y+5} \\\\ 3\\cdot (y+5) & =y\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3y+15 & =-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y+15 & =-2y \\\\ 3y+15-3y & =-2y-3y \\\\ 15 & =-5y \\\\ \\frac{15}{-5} & =\\frac{-5y}{-5} \\\\ -3 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $y=-3$ is different from $y=0$ and $y=-5$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $y=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498597 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498597 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102820" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498597 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498597 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\frac{1}{y+2}=\\frac{3}{2y+5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f11ebff6-3ffc-5ee8-b046-9fea0d3fb648" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498597 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $y=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $y=-2$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y+2} & =\\frac{3}{2y+5} \\\\ 1\\cdot (2y+5) & =(y+2)\\cdot 3 \\\\ 2y+5 & =3y+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y+5 & =3y+6 \\\\ 2y+5-2y & =3y+6-2y \\\\ 5 & =y+6 \\\\ 5-6 & =y+6-6 \\\\ -1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $y=-1$ is different from $y=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $y=-2,$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $y=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
